<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Verkhovna Rada</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Supreme Council of Ukraine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Verkhovna <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a>, or Supreme Council, is the parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, a single chamber of 450 deputies. It began as the Supreme Soviet of the Ukrainian SSR, and after the first competitive elections of 1990 it declared Ukraine's state <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> that July. On 24 August 1991 it adopted the Act of Declaration of Independence of Ukraine, confirmed by referendum on 1 December 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/verkhovna-rada.jpg" alt="Verkhovna Rada" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EricLewan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Verkhovna_Rada_(UK_logo,_2022).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
